import ../../../ui/shapes.dl

to check color channel {a number:actual} equals {a number:expected}:
    require condition ((the absolute value of (actual - expected)) < 0.000001) reporting "Shared sRGB conversion or linear paint data changed."

set view to a new UI view
set target to the address of view
set view's linear colors to false
check color channel (the UI color channel 128 in target) equals (128.0 / 255.0)
set view's linear colors to true
check color channel (the UI color channel 0 in target) equals 0.0
check color channel (the UI color channel 255 in target) equals 1.0
check color channel (the UI color channel 128 in target) equals 0.21586050011389926
check color channel (the UI color channel 10 in target) equals ((10.0 / 255.0) / 12.92)
set gray to linear UI ink from (UI ink 128 128 128)
check color channel (gray's red) equals (the UI color channel 128 in target)
set first to linear UI ink red 0.0 green 0.2 blue 0.4
set second to linear UI ink red 1.0 green 0.6 blue 0.8
set mixed to linear UI ink between first and second at 0.5
check color channel (mixed's red) equals 0.5
check color channel (mixed's green) equals 0.4
check color channel (mixed's blue) equals 0.6
print line "UI painting and scene data share sRGB conversion and portable linear RGB values."
